      {
        "id": 214291,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-02-19T19:49:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Bigbywolfe\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/dbc845/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Bigbywolfe:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Has the “errata” on BUDDABUDDABUDDABUDDA ever been confirmed officially? A player pointed out that the Ability reads: “<strong>Whenever you Attack</strong>, either Attack one target with Max+Min dice, or Attack two different targets, one with your Max die and one with your Mid die.” and argued that this effect would be <strong>in addition</strong>&nbsp;to whatever <strong>other</strong>&nbsp;attack you were performing. Considering every other Attack Ability Bunker has is labeled as an Action and says Attack X targets, or Attack using X Power, it would seem that the wording “Whenever you attack” was chosen intentionally because it gave an additional effect while in Turret mode and that the Ability is not just an additional, seperate Attack Action option.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Unfortunately I wasn’t in the habit of citing my sources when I started this thread, but yes, that’s official.&nbsp; BUDDABUDDABUDDA should be an Action and cannot be combined with other abilities.&nbsp; That’s why it’s errata and not just a clarification, because your player would be absolutely right otherwise.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:45:27.601Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
